Mavio's patch to start the coreaudio output where macOS refuses the
channel layout mpv gives as the output unit's channel map
(kAudioOutputUnitProperty_ChannelMap answers paramErr, -50, on macOS 27):
a warning instead of a failure, the unit mapping the channels in order.
Without it mpv falls back to the avfoundation output, which queues two
seconds of audio, so that mute and the volume take that long to be heard,
and a coreaudio device chosen plays nothing. Against mpv 88eb9f2;
scripts/build-mpv-macos.sh applies it with git apply, which skips this
header.

diff --git a/audio/out/ao_coreaudio.c b/audio/out/ao_coreaudio.c
index 7d42139..6bff9bb 100644
--- a/audio/out/ao_coreaudio.c
+++ b/audio/out/ao_coreaudio.c
@@ -327,8 +327,9 @@ static bool init_audiounit(struct ao *ao, AudioStreamBasicDescription asbd, Audi
                                kAudioOutputUnitProperty_ChannelMap,
                                kAudioUnitScope_Global, 0, layout, layout_size);
 
-    CHECK_CA_ERROR_L(coreaudio_error_audiounit,
-                     "unable to set the input channel layout on the audio unit");
+    // macOS 27 refuses the layout as a channel map (paramErr); the unit
+    // then maps the channels in order, which suits stereo.
+    CHECK_CA_WARN("unable to set the input channel layout on the audio unit");
 
     AURenderCallbackStruct render_cb = (AURenderCallbackStruct) {
         .inputProc       = render_cb_lpcm,
